// CLYDE — "Crystallized Loop Yarn Desolation Emergence"
// Virtual HDMI synchronization protocol · Sovereign Core Matrix
//
// Owner canon: CLYDE is the sync spine — phone as master clock, five real
// pipeline phases (Crystallized → Loop → Yarn → Desolation → Emergence),
// software virtual-HDMI timing model, sync targets monitor/headset/internal.
//
// HONEST ARCHITECTURE (read before touching):
// - Browsers cannot access real EDID hardware, emit real HDMI, or control
//   OS-level clocks. The "virtual HDMI profile" is a SOFTWARE TIMING MODEL:
//   standard HDMI timing parameters computed in code (hTotal/vTotal/pixel
//   clock), used to derive the frame clock. It is labeled as such everywhere.
// - "Phone as master clock" = the browser's best available clock:
//   AudioContext.currentTime (sample-accurate, audio-hardware driven, lowest
//   jitter) when an AudioContext exists, performance.now() otherwise.
// - The five phases are REAL pipeline stages, not labels: each one runs code
//   every scheduler tick (see tick()). Phase state is inspectable live via
//   getPhases().
// - Module scope is DOM-free (node-importable). Browser APIs are touched only
//   inside init()/startLoop(), guarded with typeof checks.
